Summary: Install placeholder AMD and NVIDIA DLLs in 64-bit prefixes, for D3DMetal and DXMT
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Origin: crossover
  Version: 26.3.0
  CW-Hacks: 22435
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
  Note: CrossOver 26.3.0 CW HACK 22435, the wine.inf part (loader/wine.inf.in)
    Source: (sources/wine/loader/wine.inf.in)
Upstream: no
Why: Have wineboot put placeholder nvapi64.dll and nvngx.dll in a 64-bit
 prefix's system32. No builtin DLLs have those names, so setupapi writes generic
 placeholder DLLs; with one in system32, DXMT's nvapi64.dll and nvngx.dll on its
 DLL path (WINEDLLPATH_DXMT) can be loaded, which Wine otherwise refuses outside
 prefix setup. The 10.0 copy also adds atidxx64.dll, for D3DMetal: D3DMetal 3.0
 needs Wine 10.4's GSBASE model, so it is supported on 10.0 only (from Wine
 10.5, WineHQ 3a16aabb, it crashes when a program creates a DXGI factory;
 measured on 11.22).
Programs: none known
Evidence: Sikarugir 10.0_8: its share/wine/wine.inf has these lines with this
 comment; it is the only difference in share/.
Port: the 10.0 copy's lines without atidxx64.dll, which only D3DMetal ships
Status: 11.21, 11.22: 2026-11-26: atidxx64.dll dropped (D3DMetal can't run on
 11.x); not yet in a build

diff --git a/loader/wine.inf.in b/loader/wine.inf.in
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -746,6 +746,9 @@ HKLM,SOFTWARE\Microsoft\VisualStudio\14.0\VC\Runtimes\x86,"Version",2,"14.51.362
 [FakeDllsWin64]
 10,twain_64,sane.ds
 10,twain_64,gphoto2.ds
+; CW HACK 22435: fake DLLs for D3DMetal, here only DXMT's (D3DMetal needs Wine 10.4)
+11,,nvapi64.dll,*
+11,,nvngx.dll,*
 
 ; Wow64-only fake dlls
 [FakeDllsWow64]
